1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,111
Bring your own CSV.

2
00:00:02,111 --> 00:00:05,981
Preview your inputs and exchange rates, then create linked revenue reports.

3
00:00:05,981 --> 00:00:09,445
This CSV example has two rows.

4
00:00:09,445 --> 00:00:13,864
In the separate guided demo, correct the euro exchange rate.

5
00:00:13,864 --> 00:00:16,515
Revenue becomes stale and is withheld.

6
00:00:16,515 --> 00:00:22,467
The independent support count stays current, while previous revenue remains clearly historical.

7
00:00:22,467 --> 00:00:29,942
HydraDB traces the inputs each tool actually consumed, linking this calculation to both reports.

8
00:00:29,942 --> 00:00:32,917
Four tools refresh the dependent work.

9
00:00:32,917 --> 00:00:37,379
Company revenue becomes five thousand seven hundred fifty-five dollars;

10
00:00:37,379 --> 00:00:41,346
EU revenue, two thousand two hundred eighty.

11
00:00:41,346 --> 00:00:43,484
Independent recomputation matches.

12
00:00:43,484 --> 00:00:48,785
After a correction, an analyst needs to know which reports can still be used.

13
00:00:48,785 --> 00:00:54,087
We tested that on eight retail cases, with 48 Fable 5.2 runs.

14
00:00:54,087 --> 00:00:55,980
The model proposes a plan;

15
00:00:55,980 --> 00:00:58,902
the same tools handle every refresh.

16
00:00:58,902 --> 00:01:04,112
Graph, exact traversal, and full context refreshed all 32 recoverable reports.

17
00:01:04,112 --> 00:01:07,427
Every method blocked all four unavailable reports.

18
00:01:07,427 --> 00:01:10,918
No incorrect report was marked current.

19
00:01:10,918 --> 00:01:17,344
Graph used 60.67% fewer input tokens than full context, excluding the no-op.

20
00:01:17,344 --> 00:01:21,608
Graph and exact traversal gave the model identical prompts.

21
00:01:21,608 --> 00:01:26,606
The model test used one sample per case and method, with adaptive allowances.

22
00:01:26,606 --> 00:01:29,681
An earlier deterministic test fell short at a

23
00:01:29,681 --> 00:01:33,022
fixed cap and failed its development gate.

24
00:01:33,022 --> 00:01:37,542
An actual Claude client uses five MCP tools

25
00:01:37,542 --> 00:01:41,157
to load data, choose plans, inspect and refresh.

26
00:01:41,157 --> 00:01:44,773
It reuses prior artifacts on authored two-row input.

27
00:01:44,773 --> 00:01:48,841
After a launch-configuration fix, one trajectory passed 32 checks,

28
00:01:48,841 --> 00:01:52,457
with nine requests and twelve recorded runtime calls.

29
00:01:52,457 --> 00:01:55,819
Its first configuration failure is retained.

30
00:01:55,819 --> 00:02:00,000
ProofFlow: current evidence across agent runs.
